{"kind":"request","text":"Make every valid `#N` reference in user-visible prose navigate to the durable event at ticket N. Ticket numbers are already the human handle for log positions and explicit Ticket/RestsOn controls navigate correctly, but numbers embedded in ordinary statement text, conditions, topic/work summaries, profile excerpts, temporary discussion, and similar prose remain inert.\n\nIntroduce one shared safe prose-tokenization/rendering path that composes ticket references with the existing @mention presentation. Build ticket resolution from the current projection's complete event-to-ticket order and resolve only a syntactically complete `#` plus positive decimal number whose ticket exists in that projection. A known reference uses the same canonical event navigation as the existing Ticket control; it is keyboard-focusable, visibly interactive, exposes the full event identifier or useful destination label accessibly, and stops row/card selection so the referenced event wins. An unknown, zero, malformed, embedded, or out-of-range number remains ordinary text exactly as written.\n\nApply the renderer to all user-authored prose surfaces, including durable statement titles/bodies, conditions and other displayed prose body fields, topic and work-item summaries, profile recent text, artifact/inspector prose, notifications, temporary frames, and their thread/railway renderings. Do not rewrite editors while typing, code/preformatted content, identifiers, repository paths, commit hashes, URLs, or the explicit Ticket components that already represent their own event. Preserve whitespace, punctuation, line wrapping, mention highlighting, retired styling, truncation, search text, and screen-reader reading order.\n\nAvoid invalid nested interactive markup in clickable rows and cards: restructure their hit targets where necessary, and verify that clicking or activating an embedded reference opens the referenced event rather than the containing item. Cover repeated and adjacent references, punctuation and line breaks, the first and last ticket, unknown/future tickets, `#0`, leading zeroes, very large digit strings, `abc#12`, URL fragments, Markdown/code-like text where applicable, @mentions beside tickets, stale projection replacement, keyboard activation, focus indication, and event navigation from every representative surface.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-ticket-reference-links","conditions":"Every syntactically complete positive `#N` token in user-authored prose becomes a keyboard-accessible link when N resolves in the current durable projection and uses canonical event navigation; unknown, zero, malformed, embedded, out-of-range, identifier/path/hash/URL, editor, code, and explicit-Ticket cases remain unchanged; statement text, displayed conditions/body prose, topic/work summaries, profile excerpts, artifact/inspector/notification prose, temporary discussion, thread and railway representative surfaces share one renderer that preserves mentions, whitespace, punctuation, wrapping, truncation, styling, search, and reading order; embedded references win over containing row/card actions without nested interactive markup; boundary, multiple-reference, projection-refresh, pointer/keyboard/focus/accessibility, component, DOM, UI build, embed-drift, and repository tests pass.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}